        "original_id": "a6fd10f3-d90a-59c7-82ae-4af43bfa7fe7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rachel Jacobs\n- Companies: ApprenNet, Amtrak\n- Events: 2015 Philadelphia train derailment\n- Places: New York, Philadelphia, Port Richmond, Pennsylvania, Washington, D.C.\n\nFacts:\n- Rachel Jacobs was born on October 3, 1975, and she was an American social entrepreneur and technology company CEO.\n- Rachel Jacobs had recently joined ApprenNet, an educational technology company, as CEO by May 2015.\n- On May 12, 2015, an Amtrak Northeast Regional train traveling from Washington, D.C., to New York City derailed on the Northeast Corridor in the Port Richmond neighborhood of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.\n- Rachel Jacobs was killed at age 39 in the May 12, 2015, Philadelphia train derailment while commuting between her home in New York and ApprenNet’s Philadelphia offices.",
